\section*{Bases of projective Lagrangian fibrations}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Every projective Lagrangian fibration of a compact Kähler IHS manifold is claimed to have projective space as its base. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 041, 2026-09-23): The first stage excludes nonquotient singularities using fixed-base deformations, Euler obstructions, and Hodge variation. A finite abelian cover and a second varying fibration eliminate the residual quotient stabilizers, establishing smoothness before the known smooth-base theorem is applied.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
